From: omarchy-m5 <omarchy-m5@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backend: allocate graphics buffers on the resolved render node

A display-only KMS device can resolve to a separate render GPU. Reopening
its primary DRM descriptor still yields the display device, which cannot
create a hardware GBM allocator. Prefer the existing render-node descriptor
for the primary and auxiliary GBM allocators, matching the renderer's own
device selection. Keep the primary descriptor for KMS, polling and leases.

Include cmath directly for std::round when building with the target's
GCC 16.1.1 C++ headers rather than relying on transitive includes.

Base: Aquamarine v0.16.0 (b77d67648336223a6c8fb88844ae316e7b72b574).

---
diff --git i/src/backend/Backend.cpp w/src/backend/Backend.cpp
index dbd7147..7924fbf 100644
--- i/src/backend/Backend.cpp
+++ w/src/backend/Backend.cpp
@@ -161,8 +161,10 @@ bool Aquamarine::CBackend::start() {
 
     // TODO: obviously change this when (if) we add different allocators.
     for (auto const& b : implementations) {
-        if (b->drmFD() >= 0) {
-            auto fd = reopenDRMNode(b->drmFD());
+        const int renderFD    = b->drmRenderNodeFD();
+        const int allocatorFD = renderFD >= 0 ? renderFD : b->drmFD();
+        if (allocatorFD >= 0) {
+            auto fd = reopenDRMNode(allocatorFD);
             if (fd < 0) {
                 // this is critical, we cannot create an allocator properly
                 log(AQ_LOG_CRITICAL, "Failed to create an allocator (reopenDRMNode failed)");
